/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.log
.ingest_cache
# Run-history index. Lives beside the report, so a run using the default --report-path drops it
# in whatever directory it was launched from -- including this one.
.rustcopy_history.jsonl
.rustcopy_history.*.jsonl
robocopy_ingest.log
robocopy_ingest_report.json
*.html
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/.graphify_*
# Only /graphify-out (repo root) is the canonical graph, tracked deliberately (graph.json +
# GRAPH_REPORT.md). A graphify-out/ anywhere else, at any depth, is a stray graph from running
# `graphify extract <subdir>/` instead of `/graphify --update` on the root -- ignore it outright
# rather than let it get committed as a second, divergent graph (see AGENTS.md's Graphify note).
# The negation only re-includes the literal root path (`!/graphify-out/`, anchored) -- it does not
# affect the nested case, verified empirically (git check-ignore) before relying on it here.
**/graphify-out/
!/graphify-out/
_ops_reports/
scripts/*.local.ps1
scripts/profiles.json
examples/*.local.toml
installer-output/
installer/Output/

# GUI (F53): the JS toolchain is confined to crates/rustcopy-gui/ui.
crates/rustcopy-gui/ui/node_modules/
crates/rustcopy-gui/ui/dist/
# The blanket `*.html` above exists for generated report output. The GUI's entry point is
# source, not output, and without this negation it was silently untracked: the build worked
# locally, where the file existed, and failed in CI with "0 modules transformed".
!crates/rustcopy-gui/ui/index.html
# Regenerated by tauri-build on every compilation.
crates/rustcopy-gui/gen/schemas/
